tmp/
CLAUDE.md

# Quran corpus — raw Tanzil downloads are reproducible. Per-surah
# files under data/surahs/ are committed; only the source/ inputs
# the import script reads from are skipped.
src/quran/data/source/
# Build artifacts — NEVER commit APKs, AABs, or IPAs to this repo.
# They bloat git history and broke F-Droid CI clones (856MB pack, 2026-05).
# Upload release artifacts to GitHub Releases only.
*.apk
*.aab
*.ipa

# Device dumps — NEVER commit these. A bugreport is a 38MB transcript of
# everything the phone was doing: full logcat, every installed package,
# wifi state, system API keys. One was committed on 2026-09-01 and pushed
# to a public repo before anyone noticed. Nothing here belongs in git.
bugreport*.zip
bugreport*.txt
*.hprof
anr_*
dumpstate*
# Loose archives, which is the shape every one of those arrives in.
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz

# Quran reader debug scratch (screenshots, geometry sources)
.qr-data/
branding/tools/__pycache__/
.ipadshots/
.shots/
outputs/triage/
build/shots/
build/qcf*/

# Developer ID profile for the Catalyst build — account-specific, not source.
# See the PROFILE note in scripts/build-catalyst.sh.
ios/PrayerApp/embedded.provisionprofile

# This machine's account of its own release attempts — evidence for the
# release log, not a repo fact.
.release-attempts.log

# Python bytecode caches. One was committed and then rewritten by any
# tool that imported scripts/xcode-cloud.py, which is a dirty tree the
# release script correctly refuses to build from.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Riwayah datasets used to live under src/quran/data/<riwayah>/ and be
# ignored here. They do not live anywhere in the repository now: the app
# ships no Warsh text at all, because nobody publishes one under terms it
# could be redistributed under. A reader obtains the muṣḥaf from whoever
# publishes it and it lands on their device — see src/quran/riwayahStore.ts
# and docs/design/riwayat-plan.md §0. There is nothing left to ignore.
